(Abstract) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(Knowledge workers now swim in notification density that would have looked like a paging) Tj
0 -13 Td
(storm a decade ago. We asked whether that density predicts what people can actually recall) Tj
0 -13 Td
(from documents they were supposed to have read. Across 312 remote employees in twelve firms,) Tj
0 -13 Td
(we found that each additional ten non-urgent notifications per hour during a reading block) Tj
0 -13 Td
(was associated with an 18 percent drop in delayed recall of the assigned paper. The effect) Tj
0 -13 Td
(held after we accounted for sleep, role seniority, and self-reported interest in the topic.) Tj
0 -13 Td
(A protected quiet hour cut notification density by 72 percent and recovered most of the lost) Tj
0 -13 Td
(recall. We argue that civic and workplace reading is failing less because people are lazy) Tj
0 -13 Td
(and more because the channel is too loud. Limitations include a convenience sample and a) Tj
0 -13 Td
(two-week window. Still, the practical claim is blunt: if you want people to remember a) Tj
0 -13 Td
(paper, stop tapping them while they read it.) Tj
0 -13 Td
( ) Tj
0 -8 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F3 13 Tf
(1. Introduction) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(Organizations still assign papers. They still hold briefings. They still ask staff to come) Tj
0 -13 Td
(back next week having understood a 30-page PDF. Meanwhile the same staff keep Slack, mail,) Tj
0 -13 Td
(and calendar banners alive on the same screen. This paper treats that collision as a) Tj
0 -13 Td
(measurement problem rather than a sermon about willpower.) Tj
0 -13 Td
( ) Tj
0 -8 Td
(We use the phrase civic attention decay for a simple pattern: as interruptive cues rise, the) Tj
0 -13 Td
(share of a document that can be recalled a few hours later falls, even when people report) Tj
0 -13 Td
(that they finished the file. The civic part matters. City staff, newsroom reporters, and) Tj
0 -13 Td
(nonprofit analysts are often the people asked to read long public documents under the worst) Tj
0 -13 Td
(notification climates.) Tj
0 -13 Td
( ) Tj
0 -8 Td
(Prior work on task switching shows costs in the range of several hundred milliseconds per) Tj
0 -13 Td
(switch, which sounds small until it is multiplied by a hundred pings. Our contribution is) Tj
0 -13 Td
(not another lab task with colored shapes. We handed people real documents, counted real) Tj
0 -13 Td
(workplace notifications, and then quizzed them on claims that actually appeared in the text.) Tj
0 -13 Td
( ) Tj
0 -8 Td
( ) Tj
0 -12 Td
/F3 13 Tf
(2. Methods) Tj
0 -16 Td
/F1 11 Tf
(We recruited 312 knowledge workers through professional networks in public agencies,) Tj
0 -13 Td
(newsrooms, and software firms. Median age was 34. Fifty-four percent identified as women.) Tj
0 -13 Td
(Participants were not paid beyond a summary of their own team's results.) Tj
0 -13 Td
( ) Tj
0 -8 Td
(Each person received a 2,400-word briefing paper on congestion pricing, chosen because it is) Tj
0 -13 Td
(dense, civic, and unfamiliar to most private-sector staff. They had 40 minutes to read it on) Tj
0 -13 Td
