(Notification density was measured from OS-level notification logs that participants exported) Tj
0 -13 Td
(themselves, plus Slack analytics where available. We counted banners, sounds, and badge) Tj
0 -13 Td
(bumps that occurred during the 40-minute reading window. We excluded notifications the) Tj
0 -13 Td
(participant had explicitly classified as urgent in a pre-survey, so a page from a child's) Tj
0 -13 Td
(school still counted as urgent and was removed from the density score.) Tj
0 -13 Td
( ) Tj
0 -8 Td
(Recall was a 16-item short-answer quiz administered four hours later. Items were drawn from) Tj
0 -13 Td
(the briefing: three numbers, five named mechanisms, four caveats, and four who-said-what) Tj
0 -13 Td
(attributions. Two raters scored answers against a rubric. Agreement was high \(Cohen's kappa) Tj
0 -13 Td
(= 0.84\).) Tj
0 -13 Td
( ) Tj
0 -8 Td
(In week two, six of the twelve firms ran a quiet hour: 90 minutes of calendar-busy time with) Tj
0 -13 Td
(Slack set to notifications-off except for a named emergency channel. The other six firms) Tj
0 -13 Td
(were waitlisted. Assignment was at the firm level, not the person level, which we treat as a) Tj
0 -13 Td
(limitation rather than a feature.) Tj
0 -13 Td
